WEBVTT

01:26.980 --> 01:29.440
I can't cut this!

01:32.320 --> 01:34.570
And now it's stuck!

01:40.240 --> 01:43.830
Why do squashes have such a hard skin?

01:43.830 --> 01:45.950
Oh! I remember a cooking program saying that

01:45.950 --> 01:48.790
if you warm it up in a microwave first, it'd be easier to slice!

01:50.540 --> 01:52.250
What?! The microwave's not here!

01:52.840 --> 01:57.050
Now that I think about it, the pot, the ladle, and the colander are missing too!

01:57.420 --> 01:59.510
I wonder where they are...

01:59.510 --> 02:02.010
Wanya, have you seen the brush used to clean the bath?

02:02.010 --> 02:02.550
What?!

02:02.550 --> 02:04.890
The wash basin and bucket are missing too...

02:05.600 --> 02:08.310
We're missing quite a few items here too.

02:08.310 --> 02:11.940
What? Could this be Ruu-kun's fault?

02:14.150 --> 02:18.360
You're missing your water gun too?

02:18.360 --> 02:19.440
What's going on?

02:21.080 --> 02:26.120
Inventions are Boring

02:28.580 --> 02:29.540
What is it?

02:30.210 --> 02:31.420
What's going on?

02:31.420 --> 02:32.130
Wanya.

02:32.130 --> 02:33.090
Wanya!

02:35.050 --> 02:37.090
I hope it's not a thief...

02:39.220 --> 02:40.430
Ready?

02:40.430 --> 02:42.010
Y-Yes.

02:51.850 --> 02:53.310
What's this?

02:53.310 --> 02:56.230
Kanata-san, Santa-san, and even Nozomu-san...

02:56.860 --> 02:57.570
Yo!

02:57.570 --> 02:58.740
Hi, Miyu-cchi.

02:58.740 --> 03:02.450
My, my... what on earth are you making?

03:02.450 --> 03:05.330
Look! The oven's here!

03:05.330 --> 03:07.870
Sorry, we need to use the microwave for a while.

03:08.290 --> 03:10.410
Santa-san, what is<i> this?</i>

03:10.410 --> 03:11.370
Who are you?

03:11.370 --> 03:14.290
Um... he's the child of a relative we're currently taking care of.

03:14.290 --> 03:14.880
I see.

03:15.340 --> 03:18.260
Don't be surprised. This is our secret project!

03:18.260 --> 03:18.840
Wait there a sec.

03:22.510 --> 03:23.680
So, don't be surprised.

03:23.680 --> 03:28.720
This is the Crack-a-squash-peel-it-
remove-the-seeds-and-seed-planting-machine.

03:28.720 --> 03:33.100
The "Crack-a-squash-peel-it-
remove-the-seeds-and-seed-planting-machine"?

03:33.100 --> 03:35.480
And? What does this machine do?

03:35.480 --> 03:39.190
It's a machine that cracks a squash, peels it, removes the seeds, and then plants them.

03:39.190 --> 03:41.490
We're still thinking up a good name for it.

03:41.490 --> 03:46.830
For example, "Kaboccha!," or like "Kabon Kabon," or maybe even "Kabocchi Kabocchi."

03:41.490 --> 03:46.830
[Note: "Kabocha" translates to "squash" or "pumpkin" in Japanese.]

03:46.830 --> 03:48.660
They all seem rather boring.

03:48.660 --> 03:50.910
But it sounds really useful.

03:50.910 --> 03:53.710
It's a real hassle to cook squash dishes.

03:53.710 --> 03:54.170
Exactly.

03:54.540 --> 03:58.380
At first it was supposed to be a Crack-a-
watermelon-peel-it-remove-the-seeds-machine,

03:58.380 --> 04:01.670
but Kanata insisted we design it for squashes instead, so...

04:01.670 --> 04:04.090
Then I suggested that since it was going to remove the seeds anyway,

04:04.090 --> 04:06.720
we might as well get it to plant them too.

04:06.720 --> 04:09.520
The three of us agreed with each other straight away.

04:09.520 --> 04:10.060
Yes!

04:10.060 --> 04:11.060
Yeah!

04:12.520 --> 04:15.060
Okay, Ruu. Watch this.

04:18.440 --> 04:20.400
Switch on.

04:36.330 --> 04:37.670
W-What's happening?

04:40.630 --> 04:41.550
Duck!

04:50.100 --> 04:52.890
Though, we still need to improve it a little.

04:52.890 --> 04:55.640
There's no way we can use this!

04:54.480 --> 04:56.600
It's wonderful.

04:56.600 --> 04:59.610
If only I had such a machine at home...

04:59.650 --> 05:02.150
Actually, there's going to be

05:02.150 --> 05:03.820
an Inventions Contest at Heio City Shopping District.

05:03.820 --> 05:04.950
Really?

05:04.950 --> 05:09.780
If we win, this Crack-a-squash-peel-it-
remove-the-seeds-and-seed-planting-machine

05:09.780 --> 05:12.040
will be commercialized and sold in Tarafuku Supermarket.

05:12.040 --> 05:13.620
What? Really?

05:13.620 --> 05:14.200
Yup.

05:14.200 --> 05:16.330
There may come a time when there's a Crack-a-squash-peel-it

05:16.330 --> 05:18.290
remove-the-seeds-and-seed-planting-
machine in every household.

05:18.290 --> 05:22.050
He really goes crazy over squashes, eh?

05:22.050 --> 05:25.260
I guess a girl just doesn't understand these things.

05:25.260 --> 05:27.800
This is a man's dream!

05:27.800 --> 05:29.180
It's just beautiful.

05:29.850 --> 05:31.430
It's amazing!

05:31.430 --> 05:33.220
It's very exciting!

05:33.890 --> 05:35.140
I want one too.

05:36.100 --> 05:37.600
An Inventions Contest?

05:38.730 --> 05:40.440
Now that you mention it,

05:40.440 --> 05:44.320
those three have been hanging around more than usual and acting rather suspiciously.

05:44.740 --> 05:45.360
So...

05:45.360 --> 05:47.150
Oh, that's...

05:48.200 --> 05:49.280
They're too suspicious.

05:49.660 --> 05:51.830
I envy them.

05:51.830 --> 05:52.700
Chris-chan?

05:53.080 --> 05:58.420
Male friendship... A sacred world that girls cannot enter.

05:58.420 --> 06:04.590
Ah! If possible, I'd love to join them.

06:04.590 --> 06:06.050
Why don't you?

06:06.590 --> 06:11.600
But they're making a Crack-a-squash-peel-it-
remove-the-seeds-and-seed-planting-machine.

06:11.600 --> 06:12.530
Squash...

06:12.530 --> 06:13.500
Crack...

06:14.100 --> 06:15.220
Peel it...

06:15.220 --> 06:16.600
Remove the seeds...

06:16.600 --> 06:18.140
And plant them?

06:18.140 --> 06:19.980
That doesn't excite me.

06:20.520 --> 06:22.690
This is amazing, Doria nee-chan.

06:22.690 --> 06:25.190
They say the winning invention will be commercialized

06:25.190 --> 06:27.700
and sold in Tarafuku Supermarket.

06:27.700 --> 06:30.570
And then people will buy lots of our stuff

06:30.570 --> 06:32.660
even if we don't advertise on the streets like we did in the past.

06:32.660 --> 06:35.700
I bet we'll pay off our debt in no time!

06:35.700 --> 06:36.700
Of course!

06:36.700 --> 06:37.000
Yay!

06:37.000 --> 06:40.210
Though I don't particularly like the thought of people who call themselves

06:40.210 --> 06:43.130
members of the Waru Waru Gang participating in such an unprofitable venture...

06:43.130 --> 06:46.170
But, Doria nee-chan, you're a professional inventor, right?

06:46.170 --> 06:48.220
Even if I am...

06:48.220 --> 06:51.890
Is it possible that you're not confident, Doria nee-chan?

06:52.800 --> 06:57.220
Well, it's true that we can't be certain that you'll win...

06:57.850 --> 07:00.100
I'll do it!

07:00.100 --> 07:03.480
I'll show you the true power of evil!

07:06.280 --> 07:09.190
I was planning to get Kanata to help me with the shopping,

07:09.190 --> 07:11.030
but he's really good at making quick escapes.

07:11.030 --> 07:13.870
Wanya, can you make me some tea?

07:15.370 --> 07:16.620
Wanya?

07:17.370 --> 07:19.160
Ruu-kun?

07:19.160 --> 07:21.080
I wonder if they're out.

07:32.720 --> 07:35.220
Even Ruu-kun and Wanya are helping them...

07:35.220 --> 07:37.720
You're doing good, Ruu. That's a boy.

07:38.640 --> 07:43.350
So this is the rumored Crack-a-squash-peel-
it-remove-the-seeds-and-seed-planting-machine?

07:43.350 --> 07:44.770
Does it really work?

07:44.770 --> 07:48.610
So this is what Ruu is secretly up to after canceling our date.

07:48.610 --> 07:49.940
Everyone!

07:50.530 --> 07:52.570
It sounded interesting, so we came to check it out.

07:52.950 --> 07:56.490
All right, Ruu-kun, switch it on for me.

07:52.950 --> 07:56.490
It worked!

08:06.630 --> 08:07.840
Duck!

08:14.930 --> 08:16.550
It failed...

08:16.550 --> 08:19.930
I wonder if the problem is the angle of the water pistol and the water pressure.

08:19.930 --> 08:22.310
I don't think that's the problem.

08:22.810 --> 08:28.320
My, my, if it isn't the ladies. Did you all come because you were worried about me...

08:28.770 --> 08:31.820
Ruu-kun, you shouldn't be in such a dangerous place.

08:31.820 --> 08:32.650
Let's go.

08:34.030 --> 08:34.990
Ruu-kun...

08:36.570 --> 08:39.330
It'll be fine. I'm watching over him.

08:39.330 --> 08:40.910
Besides, Ruu-kun's having fun.

08:41.290 --> 08:45.250
Oh, playing house is also fun, isn't it, Ruu?

08:47.380 --> 08:49.880
I smell something delicious.

08:50.460 --> 08:55.630
Um... I made mitarashi dangos as a present.

08:55.970 --> 08:58.300
Did you say mitarashi dangos?

08:58.300 --> 09:00.060
Why don't we eat them together?

09:00.060 --> 09:02.020
Thanks, Hanakomachi-san.

09:02.020 --> 09:05.060
But this place is off-limits to non-participants.

09:06.520 --> 09:10.980
Now, now, don't say such harsh things. It is mitarashi dangos we're talking about here.

09:06.520 --> 09:10.980
You never know when a spy trying to steal our invention may sneak in.

09:10.980 --> 09:12.900
We want to win this time for sure.

09:10.980 --> 09:15.070
Mitarashi dangos are so delicious. It's like they came from another world.

09:12.900 --> 09:15.070
That's why we're going to be extra cautious.

09:15.070 --> 09:18.490
Don't take it too badly, ladies.

09:18.780 --> 09:21.490
Is that so? Then suit yourselves!

09:22.540 --> 09:24.710
At least leave the mitarashi dangos!

09:24.710 --> 09:25.910
Ow!

09:27.880 --> 09:29.590
I made them with love for Kanata-kun too...

09:29.590 --> 09:31.710
That was really rude.

09:33.260 --> 09:34.880
I'll never root for them!

09:35.220 --> 09:40.890
Fine! The boys can just stick together, we don't need them.

09:42.310 --> 09:45.680
I wonder if they can really win with something like that.

09:46.390 --> 09:50.770
No one would want a Crack-a-squash-peel-it-
remove-the-seeds-and-seed-planting-machine.

09:50.770 --> 09:53.730
I want that...

09:54.280 --> 09:57.200
Oh, no! I need to inform Doria nee-chan of this!

10:00.910 --> 10:03.620
Okay, watch carefully.

10:03.620 --> 10:04.330
O-Okay.

10:21.680 --> 10:24.350
Success!

10:24.350 --> 10:27.430
The hard-boiled-egg-peeling-machine that I've made numerous improvements on,

10:27.430 --> 10:30.270
Tamachan Number 18, is finally-

10:27.430 --> 10:30.270
[Note: Tamachan is formed from "Tamago" which means "egg."]

10:30.270 --> 10:33.150
Considering this is such an elaborate-looking machine, this is all it does?

10:33.150 --> 10:34.270
You have a problem with that?

10:34.270 --> 10:36.900
No, I don't. But I do wonder whether we can really win with this...

10:36.900 --> 10:39.530
Nee-chan! Nee-chan! It's an emergency!

10:39.530 --> 10:41.570
Gwava, did you buy the eggs?

10:41.570 --> 10:46.370
Yup. I managed to get this many "one-
per-customer" packs by lining up multiple times.

10:46.370 --> 10:48.410
Yup, we're definitely evil.

10:48.410 --> 10:50.580
More importantly, I saw something amazing on my way home.

10:51.290 --> 10:54.210
A squash machine gun, eh?

10:54.550 --> 10:58.630
It can also form a part of the Waru Waru Gang's artillery. It'd be nice if we had one of those, right?

10:58.630 --> 11:01.140
What are you doing wanting to own an enemy's invention?!

11:03.680 --> 11:06.600
There's no way my invention will lose to the likes of them!

11:06.600 --> 11:07.600
That's right.

11:07.600 --> 11:09.600
However, there is one problem.

11:09.600 --> 11:10.140
What?

11:10.140 --> 11:12.560
The baby who comes from the Planet Otto.

11:12.860 --> 11:15.980
He could use his psychic powers and unleash an amazing move!

11:15.980 --> 11:20.610
No, according to this book, earthlings are weak against animals and babies.

11:20.610 --> 11:24.200
If that baby even smiles slightly at the judges,

11:24.200 --> 11:26.120
we have no chance of winning.

11:26.120 --> 11:27.040
Really?

11:27.040 --> 11:28.450
Of course!

11:28.450 --> 11:29.540
I wonder if it is.

11:29.540 --> 11:35.000
Now that it has come down to this, we'll have to hide that baby away throughout the contest.

11:35.000 --> 11:37.500
So in the end, that's where we end up at.

11:37.500 --> 11:40.340
We're finally starting to act how a Waru Waru Gang should be.

12:00.780 --> 12:02.860
Santa-kun. Nozomu-kun.

12:02.860 --> 12:03.950
Hi, Miyu-cchi!

12:03.950 --> 12:06.740
Hurry! We don't have much time left until the day of the contest!

12:07.240 --> 12:09.290
You're both late.

12:09.290 --> 12:12.540
We had a hard time gathering all the materials.

12:12.540 --> 12:14.540
Wow! There sure is a lot of stuff.

12:15.000 --> 12:18.300
All right! Get ready for an all-nighter today!

12:18.300 --> 12:19.340
Yeah!

13:05.010 --> 13:08.550
What's this? Only the boys are allowed to have fun now?

13:16.190 --> 13:18.110
Okay, it's complete.

13:18.110 --> 13:20.070
This time, please work well!

13:20.860 --> 13:23.570
Ruu, press the switch.

13:49.640 --> 13:51.060
We did it.

13:51.060 --> 13:54.680
It's a truly beautiful scene of seed planting.

13:54.680 --> 13:58.100
We sure worked hard to come so far.

13:58.480 --> 13:59.610
Ruu-chama.

14:03.860 --> 14:05.490
Finished!

14:07.570 --> 14:11.240
I-It's rather... amazing, Doria nee-chan.

14:12.240 --> 14:14.450
The appearance isn't the only thing amazing about it.

14:15.000 --> 14:17.210
We'll lure the baby out with a toy and...

14:32.140 --> 14:34.390
What do you think of my perfect plan?

14:35.600 --> 14:37.770
Doria nee-chan's kind of scary...

14:37.770 --> 14:41.310
It'd have been better if she put all that energy into creating the invention for the contest.

14:44.230 --> 14:46.490
The day of the contest is finally tomorrow.

14:46.490 --> 14:49.030
Miyu, you'll come and watch the contest, right?

14:49.030 --> 14:50.780
Oh? Is it tomorrow?

14:50.780 --> 14:53.530
Now that I think about it, you did mention something along those lines...

14:53.530 --> 14:56.500
But I'm not interested in it at all.

14:56.500 --> 15:00.420
Now, don't say that. Let's go together.

15:00.830 --> 15:02.080
Ruu-kun...

15:02.960 --> 15:04.290
I-I can't.

15:04.290 --> 15:06.760
I already said I'd go shopping with Nanami-chan and the others tomorrow.

15:06.760 --> 15:07.920
I can't break a promise.

15:11.260 --> 15:13.850
It's okay, Ruu. You shouldn't force her.

15:14.510 --> 15:17.810
T-That's right. Why don't you just go with the boys?

15:17.810 --> 15:22.230
They'll be sweating lots and screaming things like "Guts! Fight!" and "Let's go!"

15:22.230 --> 15:24.570
I'm bad at those sorts of things.

15:24.570 --> 15:25.270
Thank you for the meal.

15:25.650 --> 15:27.780
I'm going to have another look at the machine.

15:28.490 --> 15:30.610
We'll go too.

15:31.320 --> 15:34.200
Let's go. Pepo, let's go.

15:38.290 --> 15:40.410
Why does it always end up like this?

15:52.970 --> 15:54.640
How is it up there?

15:54.640 --> 15:55.970
Everything's ready.

15:57.640 --> 15:58.720
There they are.

15:58.720 --> 15:59.930
Now, let's begin the plan.

16:13.740 --> 16:17.160
A weird creature is following it instead of the baby...

16:17.160 --> 16:18.240
W-Wait!

16:30.090 --> 16:31.340
We're too late...

16:33.340 --> 16:37.470
Man, it's no use to us if you get caught in the trap.

16:37.470 --> 16:39.770
I'll untie you right now, so hold on.

16:39.770 --> 16:40.310
Huh?

16:56.030 --> 16:58.530
I've caught... you...

17:04.330 --> 17:06.000
I'm such an idiot.

17:06.000 --> 17:07.170
Miyu.

17:07.170 --> 17:09.710
Nanami-chan, Ayaka-chan, and even Momoka-chan!

17:09.710 --> 17:13.880
No matter what he says, Ruu will be sad if I'm not there.

17:13.880 --> 17:15.300
We came after all.

17:15.300 --> 17:19.640
I-I just happened to walk by, so...

17:19.640 --> 17:21.890
What are you talking about? You've already come this far.

17:21.890 --> 17:23.310
Nanami-chan!

17:23.310 --> 17:24.640
Come on, let's go.

17:26.480 --> 17:27.310
Okay...

17:29.110 --> 17:33.320
If Kanata-kun comes in first place, I'll give myself to him along with these flowers.

17:33.650 --> 17:36.740
Is that a little too bold? A little too bold?

17:40.330 --> 17:42.160
Isn't that... Ruu-kun?

17:42.160 --> 17:44.250
Hey, you!

17:44.250 --> 17:45.660
We've been discovered!

17:46.750 --> 17:48.130
Wait!

17:53.880 --> 17:56.380
Now, let us begin!

17:56.380 --> 17:59.510
Entry number one, please come on.

18:02.180 --> 18:03.930
What did you say? Ruu is?

18:03.930 --> 18:06.350
It must've happened when I wasn't looking...

18:06.350 --> 18:08.900
Maybe he's playing around the area somewhere?

18:08.900 --> 18:11.730
That's what I thought. I've looked around, but...

18:11.730 --> 18:13.190
We'll split up and look for him.

18:13.190 --> 18:15.860
Santa and Hikarigaoka, stay here and participate in the contest.

18:15.860 --> 18:19.570
Wait! We worked on this together.

18:19.570 --> 18:22.370
There's no point in participating in the contest if we don't go on together.

18:22.370 --> 18:23.790
I agree.

18:23.790 --> 18:28.290
Though I value ladies, I am also a man who values male friendship.

18:29.170 --> 18:30.210
Thank you.

18:30.210 --> 18:31.840
Let's look for Ruu together.

18:31.840 --> 18:32.250
Wait.

18:32.250 --> 18:32.630
Huh?

18:33.800 --> 18:34.630
Miyu.

18:34.630 --> 18:35.760
Miyu-san.

18:35.760 --> 18:38.550
Ladies, have you come to root for me?

18:38.550 --> 18:43.260
I'll look for Ruu-kun and bring him back, so make sure you all participate in the contest.

18:43.260 --> 18:45.470
You did all that work especially to enter this.

18:45.470 --> 18:47.980
Leave Ruu-kun to us.

18:47.980 --> 18:52.020
Girls are dependable when times get rough. Of course, guys are too.

18:52.020 --> 18:53.360
Miyu...

18:53.360 --> 18:54.480
Everyone...

18:56.440 --> 18:58.450
Wait!

19:01.160 --> 19:02.740
Ruu-kun?

19:02.740 --> 19:03.990
Ruu-kun?

19:07.750 --> 19:09.250
Chris... chan?

19:14.040 --> 19:14.670
Ruu-kun!

19:18.840 --> 19:21.090
Now, give me back Ruu-kun!

19:21.090 --> 19:22.850
You don't give up trying to kidnap Ruu-kun, do you?

19:22.850 --> 19:24.300
You're really bad people!

19:24.680 --> 19:26.270
We're bad.

19:26.270 --> 19:28.100
Yeah, it's because we're the Waru Waru Gang.

19:31.020 --> 19:34.980
Give him back!

19:42.110 --> 19:43.370
Here you go, Miyu-chan.

19:43.820 --> 19:44.910
Ruu-kun!

19:46.370 --> 19:52.080
Nowhere in this book did it say that it's really scary to make an earthling girl angry.

19:52.420 --> 19:55.420
Next up is entry number nine:

19:55.420 --> 19:58.010
The Crack-a-squash-peel-it-remove-
the-seeds-and-seed-planting-machine.

19:58.380 --> 19:59.630
Please come on.

20:01.380 --> 20:02.510
Kanata...

20:03.800 --> 20:04.890
It can't be helped.

20:04.890 --> 20:06.350
It's time. Let's start.

20:06.350 --> 20:08.060
Kanata!

20:10.350 --> 20:12.440
Somehow we made it on time.

20:12.440 --> 20:13.350
Ruu.

20:14.230 --> 20:16.820
Well then, please take a look at our invention.

20:16.820 --> 20:20.190
Here's a squash with seeds, but it's not a trick.

20:16.820 --> 20:20.190
[Note: This is a pun on the word "Tane" which can mean "seeds" or "tricks."]

20:20.610 --> 20:22.950
We place it in here like so...

20:22.950 --> 20:25.820
Now, Ruu, press the switch.

20:30.290 --> 20:32.540
Oh, my!

20:35.290 --> 20:36.420
It's amazing.

20:43.260 --> 20:45.300
It's wonderful.

20:52.850 --> 20:55.310
Now then, I will announce the winning team!

20:59.730 --> 21:03.530
And the winner is... The principal and his monkey!

21:04.200 --> 21:05.950
Congratulations.

21:05.950 --> 21:07.120
What?!

21:07.120 --> 21:08.370
What?!

21:08.740 --> 21:12.000
They were all amazing inventions and any one of them could've won.

21:12.000 --> 21:14.080
However, the monkey-shaped nutcracker can be commercialized immediately,

21:14.080 --> 21:18.380
therefore it was chosen as the winner.

21:20.340 --> 21:23.800
We should've watched out for animals instead of babies.

21:26.220 --> 21:28.760
Go on, Chris-chan.

21:28.760 --> 21:29.720
Okay.

21:32.850 --> 21:34.440
Great work.

21:34.440 --> 21:38.020
I initially planned to give you a bigger bouquet, but...

21:38.020 --> 21:39.020
Thank you.

21:39.020 --> 21:40.150
Oh, it's okay.

21:40.520 --> 21:44.070
Ruu, the way you pressed the switch was so cool.

21:44.070 --> 21:46.110
Everyone was cool.

21:46.110 --> 21:49.830
Men who try their best at something are wonderful.

21:49.830 --> 21:52.080
Thank you, ladies!

21:52.080 --> 21:54.250
Well then, let's go home, Miyu.

21:54.250 --> 21:55.540
What?

21:55.540 --> 21:57.460
Umm...Yeah.

22:04.970 --> 22:07.680
Is it possible that Miyu was...

22:07.680 --> 22:08.550
Want me to help?

22:08.550 --> 22:09.760
What?

22:09.760 --> 22:12.060
You're going to clean up inside, right?

22:12.060 --> 22:12.890
Yeah.

22:13.600 --> 22:16.270
It's a pity that you didn't win.

22:16.640 --> 22:20.270
But this past week's been really fun.

22:20.270 --> 22:23.900
I guess this is what you call a man's romance.

22:23.900 --> 22:25.280
Miyu, I'm sorry.

22:25.280 --> 22:25.740
What?

22:26.110 --> 22:30.910
We were so busy enjoying ourselves, it seems like we managed to exclude you.

22:32.990 --> 22:34.040
Kanata...

22:42.340 --> 22:45.630
You two! What would you like for supper tonight?

22:45.630 --> 22:48.590
We've got a lot of leftover squashes. Why don't we use those?

22:48.590 --> 22:50.550
Squashes again?

22:50.930 --> 22:52.220
Why not?

22:52.220 --> 22:53.430
Squashes are good.

22:53.430 --> 22:56.810
My, you two get along really well, don't you?

22:56.810 --> 22:57.640
What?

22:57.640 --> 22:59.850
N-No, not really, right?

22:59.850 --> 23:00.270
Yup.

23:00.650 --> 23:02.190
See? You two are...

23:03.520 --> 23:05.900
Jeez! What's this? You too, Ruu-kun?

23:06.360 --> 23:08.280
Wanya's diary:

23:08.280 --> 23:13.450
Male friendship is good from time to time, but it looks like me,

23:13.450 --> 23:19.920
Ruu-chama, and even Kanata-san prefer the company of everyone.

24:29.940 --> 24:59.990
Next Episode

24:31.820 --> 24:33.530
Oh my, Momoka-chan's rival?

24:33.530 --> 24:35.490
Is there even a three-year old who can compete with Momoka-chan?

24:35.490 --> 24:36.240
That's what I thought, but...

24:36.240 --> 24:38.740
There is one. I'm so surprised too.

24:38.740 --> 24:41.290
It's amazing. She's on the same level as Momoka-chan.

24:41.290 --> 24:43.620
Momoka's all right.

24:43.620 --> 24:46.790
Next time on Daa Daa Daa: Rival, Friend, or Love Rival?

24:46.790 --> 24:48.880
Hm... he sure is popular.

24:48.880 --> 24:50.550
As expected of Ruu-chama.

24:51.300 --> 24:53.470
Momoka's all right! All right!

24:53.470 --> 24:55.720
I'd like to just sit and watch calmly.

24:54.050 --> 24:59.990
Rival, Friend, or Love Rival?
